            //   - Multi-coupon: only a real `coupons` array re-seeds the chips, so a summary-only
            //     cart::updated can't shrink them (add/remove refreshes the chips from the server).
            //   - Single-coupon (flag off): any payload carrying `coupon` re-syncs the input, so a
            //     server-side invalidation (e.g. cart drops below the coupon minimum) that emits
            //     `coupon: ''` clears the stale code instead of leaving it stuck until a reload.
